# JANET Web
*.zip
*.tmp
*.log
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
# take-to-work / archives (built, not source)
**/Take to Work/
# runtime spool / uploads (when the server exists)
spool/
uploads/
# runtime package drop-folder (server seeds Log4j staging on boot; env-specific data)
Packages/*
# ...but the DoD trust-cert bundle IS version-tracked: the C2C Nemesis PKI-roots
# fixer and Cert Deploy auto-discover it here, so it must exist on a fresh clone
# and operator refreshes (new .cer) stay reviewable in history.
# NOTE (audit 2026-07-24): tracked in git != shipped. Since the 2026-07-17 policy
# NO certificate rides along in a take-to-work cut - Sync-TakeToWork.ps1 stages
# these folders EMPTY and fails the cut if a cert lands in the zip. The operator
# drops the bundle in on the work machine. (The old wording here claimed the
# opposite and was the only place still promising certs shipped.)
!Packages/DoD-Certs/
!Packages/DoD-Certs/**
# local spool of central-CSV logs when the share is unreachable
JanetLocal/*
# ...but the KEV seed catalog IS shipped (the KEV Cross-Check tool needs it on a
# fresh clone; operator add-kev edits are then version-trackable too)
!JanetLocal/KevCatalog.txt
# ...and the C2C Readiness baseline seed (the C2C tool needs it on a fresh clone;
# operator edits to check thresholds / DoD root thumbprints are then trackable too)
!JanetLocal/c2c-baseline.json
# ...and the Reports SLA deadline baseline (same ship-the-seed /
# track-operator-edits rationale as the ones above)
!JanetLocal/sla-baseline.json
# ...and the IAVM CVE->IAVA map seed (Reports IAVM tagging + KEV xref need it on a
# fresh clone; operator Add-IAVM edits are then version-trackable too). The SLA
# ledger + target-groups are RUNTIME state (accumulated per operator), so they are
# deliberately NOT negated - they stay ignored.
!JanetLocal/IavmMap.csv
# ...and the two seeds that were missed (audit 2026-07-24): both are editable
# BASELINES the tool needs on a fresh clone, same rationale as the ones above -
# AD Nemesis reads adto-baseline.json (account-management TO rule set) and BIOS
# Firmware reads BiosFirmwareCatalog.json (per-model firmware baseline). Without
# these negations JanetLocal/* swallowed them, so a fresh clone got no baseline
# and operator edits were untrackable.
!JanetLocal/adto-baseline.json
!JanetLocal/BiosFirmwareCatalog.json
# DoDRoots.sst stays ignored on purpose - it is a certificate store (see policy
# note above), and sla-ledger.json stays ignored as runtime state.
# machine-specific editor/preview config
.claude/
